@page "/docs/components/card"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Card
<PageTitle>Card - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Card</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="card" />
        </div>
        <p>A bordered surface built from small parts: a header, content and a footer. The header lays itself out as a grid, so adding a <code>BzCardAction</code> moves a button or menu into the top corner without any extra layout code. Set <code>Size</code> to <code>CardSize.Sm</code> when you need tighter padding.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(CardUsageExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, compose the parts you need. The header holds the title, description and an optional action, and the content and footer follow it." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of a card. `BzCard` is the surface, the header groups the title, description and corner action, and `BzCardContent` and `BzCardFooter` make up the body. Every part is optional." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="With header, content & footer" Example="typeof(CardDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Stat card" Description="A compact card with only a header and content. The badge sits in `BzCardAction`, so it lines up with the title in the top corner." Example="typeof(CardStatExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Notification" Example="typeof(CardNotificationExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With menu"
          Description="A dropdown menu opened from a ghost icon button. Put it in the header's `BzCardAction` for a menu in the top corner, or in the footer for one at the bottom."
          Example="typeof(CardMenuExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Media"
          Description="A video-style card with a full-bleed cover image, overlaid badges, an avatar, a menu and topic tags. It shows how far you can compose the parts with other components."
          Example="typeof(CardMediaExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Every part accepts `Class`. This example gives the card a branded indigo gradient, a larger radius and white text."
          Example="typeof(CardCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the text aligns to the right, the header action moves to the left corner and the footer content flips to the opposite side." Example="typeof(CardRtlExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzCard",
        new CompositionNode("BzCardHeader",
            new CompositionNode("BzCardTitle"),
            new CompositionNode("BzCardDescription"),
            new CompositionNode("BzCardAction")),
        new CompositionNode("BzCardContent"),
        new CompositionNode("BzCardFooter"));
}
